== record-Pauli: sealed spectral weights on the exchange collar ==
  closing operator E = eps * SWAP, eps = (-1)^(2m); sealed weight of a
  pair mode = (lam_a lam_b)^M * eps * swap_parity   (M = 3 periods)

  integer fiber (m = 0)  : sym weights (6): min = +1.94e-11, all >= 0;  antisym (3): min = -1.36e-05, all NEGATIVE
     -> positivity of sealed weights FORCES the SYMMETRIC (bosonic) sector:
        statistics = (-1)^(2m).  The wrong sector carries strictly
        negative sealed event weights: excluded (P7 7.6 family).

  half-integer (m = 1/2) : sym weights (6): min = -1.00e+00, all NEGATIVE;  antisym (3): min = +6.00e-11, all >= 0
     -> positivity of sealed weights FORCES the ANTISYMMETRIC (fermionic) sector:
        statistics = (-1)^(2m).  The wrong sector carries strictly
        negative sealed event weights: excluded (P7 7.6 family).

== consequences in the FORCED sectors ==
  coincidence probability P(a = b):
    forced half-integer sector: 0.00e+00   (PAULI EXCLUSION:
      an EXACT zero, derived from the sealed collar, not imposed)
    forced integer sector:      0.342986  > 0  (occupancy allowed;
      the sharp bunching law 2/(1+|<a|b>|^2) is Paper 9 Section 8)

== the wrong sector is signed: the P8/P10 failure signature ==
  half-integer twisted correlations, unprojected: site-Hankel min eig
  (N = 6) = -2.329342   SIGNED: fails the moment test -
  the wrong-statistics sector sits with the driven/non-moment sectors of
  Papers 8 and 10; projecting onto Fix(E) restores positivity:
  projected (forced) sector: site-Hankel min eig (N = 6) = -3.70e-31   (moment-class: RP)

== what this does to axiom (X) ==
  The single-valuedness clause of (X) is REPLACED by a theorem: sealed
  positivity on the exchange collar selects Fix(E).  (X) reduces to its
  association clause alone (D9a: the fiber transport is tied to the
  frame bundle).  Fermions are now AVAILABLE + POSITIVITY-RIGID: given
  a genuinely spinning fiber, wrong statistics is not merely unaesthetic
  - it assigns negative sealed event weights, the same exclusion that
  killed split-signature phases (P7 7.6) and silent arrows (P10 T3).
